# Fixed 2026-10-09, defect 511, lane b16-compiler (class improvement).
# Symptom: n handles ended and then n `if`s cost the checker the square of
# n: 3.26, 11.4 and 41.3 billion instructions at 500, 1,000 and 2,000.
# Cause: where paths met, `check/flow.hero` met every local's group, though
# a local no path changed holds on each what it held where control split.
# The walk now splits the flow where control splits and meets only the
# locals the paths changed since (`check/flow_log.hero`).
# This case: 300 handles ended, then 300 `if`s; and the shapes whose meet
# reads what a path changed under a split inside it: an `if` inside a
# branch, `match` arms, and the right side of `&&`.
extern "fixedbugs-511-handles-ended-then-three-hundred-ifs-meet-what-changed.h"
    record Cell tag hh
    function f_open() -> Cell acquires f_close
    function f_close(x: Cell consumes)
    function f_done(x: Cell consumes) -> bool

variant Pick
    left
    right

function many(c: bool) -> i64
    a0 = f_open()
    f_close(x: a0)
    a1 = f_open()
    f_close(x: a1)
